// The names __builtin_cpu_supports and __builtin_cpu_is take (#148, c_check_builtin_misc.c), and how clang's code tests
// each against libgcc's (and compiler-rt's) CPU model: BUSTER_CBUILTIN_CPU_FEATURE(name, word, bit) for a feature, the bit of
// word 0 (__cpu_model.features[0], at __cpu_model + 12) or of words 1 to 3 (__cpu_features2[0] to [2]), and
// BUSTER_CBUILTIN_CPU_NAME(name, field, value) for a vendor (field 0, __cpu_model.vendor), a CPU type (1, its type) or a
// subtype (2, its subtype) and the value clang compares it with. Generated data: the candidate names are the strings of
// LLVM 23's X86TargetParser.def (llvm-23-dev's /usr/include/llvm-23/llvm/TargetParser/X86TargetParser.def, its
// X86_FEATURE_COMPAT, X86_FEATURE and X86_MICROARCH_LEVEL rows and its X86_VENDOR, X86_CPU_TYPE and X86_CPU_SUBTYPE ones and
// their aliases), and every value is read from clang 23.1's -O0 code of a call of each (the load's offset and the mask or
// the compared value), which accepts every one of them; test-checker compares each with clang's code again
// (c_check_library_driver_test.c's check_test_cpu_model_runs, which runs both builds' tests of every name over every
// bit and value of the model).
